{
  "action": "In general, a standard system update will make all the necessary changes.",
  "cves": [
    "CVE-2026-40962",
    "CVE-2025-12343"
  ],
  "description": "Jiasheng Jiang discovered that FFmpeg incorrectly handled memory in\ncertain error-handling paths of its TensorFlow DNN backend. An attacker\ncould possibly use this issue to cause a denial of service. This issue only\naffected Ubuntu 24.04 LTS. (CVE-2025-12343)\n\nQuang Luong discovered that FFmpeg incorrectly handled certain subsample\ndata. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial of\nservice or possibly execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2026-40962)",
  "id": "USN-8469-1",
  "isummary": "Several security issues were fixed in FFmpeg.",
